        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Saskop',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Saskop or Sasku is an Estonian four-player partnership game in the Schafkopf group. A 36-card deck is used, with picture cards as permanent high trumps and the 6 of the chosen trump suit highest of all.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Derived from the German Schafkopf games brought to the Baltics in the 19th century. It evolved into a distinct Estonian folk game, adopting the name 'Lambapea' (Sheep's Head) in parallel with its German ancestor.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 players in fixed partnerships (North-South, East-West).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36-card deck (6s, 7s, 8s, 9s, 10s, J, Q, K, A).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36-card deck (6s, 7s, 8s, 9s, 10s, J, Q, K, A).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Each player receives 9 cards (the entire deck).',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Deal method: Cutter may specify how cards are dealt: 3 at a time (default), one at a time, 9 at a time, or other patterns such as covers to us, content to us, or face-up until a chosen card appears.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Single picture exchange: After the deal, a player with only one picture card (K, Q, or J) may place it face up; partner passes one card face down in exchange.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Roof signal: A player with no picture cards may signal partner (e.g. fingertips forming a roof); some groups allow it, others treat it as illegal.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
